WHY BOTH, AND WHICH ONE YOU END UP UNDER
----------------------------------------

This repository contains no VCV Rack code and no VCV artwork. Every file in it
is the copyright of Jeff McClintock, so it can be offered under either licence.

The licence of the ADAPTOR is not by itself the licence of what you BUILD with
it. The modules you compile against it carry their own terms, and a binary
combining them is a combined work:

  * Combine it with a GPL module -- VCV's Fundamental, for instance -- and the
    resulting binary is GPL-3.0-or-later, because the MODULE requires that. Take
    the adaptor under the GPL option and the combination is straightforward.

  * Combine it with a permissively-licensed module (CC0, MIT, BSD) whose
    ARTWORK is also permissive, and nothing forces the GPL on the result. Take
    the adaptor under ISC and the whole may be distributed under permissive
    terms.

ARTWORK IS A SEPARATE QUESTION AND USUALLY A STRICTER ONE. Panel graphics
routinely carry different terms from the code beside them -- VCV's own
Fundamental panels are CC BY-NC-ND 4.0. A permissive code licence is not
permission to ship the panels. Check both, per module, before you distribute.

None of this is legal advice.

